  The program starts by showing a title and making a list to save results. The user enters their name. If no name is entered, the program 
  asks again until a valid name is given. After a name is entered, the program sets up values used for prediction. It starts the number 
  in the middle and prepares to track patterns and colour choices. The program then asks ten questions. The first five questions help 
  predict the number by increasing or decreasing the score based on the user’s answers. The next five questions help predict the 
  favourite colour by adding points to different colour options. After all questions are answered, the program finishes the prediction. 
  It makes sure the number stays in the correct range and selects the colour with the highest score. The program then shows the result 
  with the user’s name, predicted number, and predicted colour, and saves it. Finally, the program resets so another user can repeat the 
  process.
